---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CapmLab from "../../components/CapmLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CAPM & the Security Market Line"
  description="An interactive Capital Asset Pricing Model tool: measure beta from a return scatter, then see how beta prices assets on the Security Market Line."
>
  <section class="container cl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>CAPM: the price of market risk</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Diversification leaves you holding one risk you can't escape: the market's.
      The Capital Asset Pricing Model says that's the <em>only</em> risk you get
      paid for — and it prices every asset by a single number, its
      <strong>beta</strong>. Here you can measure beta from data, then watch it
      set the fair return.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container cl-host">
    <CapmLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container cl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How the two panels connect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Left — measuring beta.</strong> Each dot is one period: the
          market's return across, the asset's up the side. The line's
          <strong>slope is beta</strong> (how much the asset amplifies the
          market) and its <strong>intercept is alpha</strong> (return the market
          doesn't explain). Turn up the noise and R² falls — that extra scatter
          is diversifiable risk you aren't paid for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right — pricing with beta.</strong> The Security Market Line
          runs from the risk-free rate through the market at β = 1. An asset
          <em>on</em> the line is fairly priced; your asset sits <em>off</em> it
          by exactly its alpha. Above the line it's a bargain; below, it's dear.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Beta is measured with error.</strong> Hit <strong>New
          sample</strong> (or switch to Live) and watch the estimate β̂ jump
          around the true β — then raise the sample size and watch it settle.
          Real-world betas carry exactly this uncertainty.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where CAPM breaks down</h2>
      <p>
        CAPM is beautiful and mostly wrong in the details. Decades of data show
        beta explains far less than it should: low-beta stocks have beaten it,
        and whole categories — small companies, cheap "value" stocks — earn more
        than their beta can justify. Those persistent gaps are unexplained
        <em>alpha</em> to CAPM, and they're exactly what multi-factor models like
        Fama–French were built to capture. That's the next chapter.
      </p>
      <p>
        Educational only, not advice. The market portfolio here is the same
        tangency portfolio you can build in the
        <a href="/tools/portfolio">Portfolio Diversification Lab</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="capm" />

  <NextTool current="/tools/capm" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .cl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .cl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .cl-group {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin: var(--space-xs) 0 0;
  }
  .cl-group:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .cl-stage {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .cl-stage {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  .cl-panel {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .cl-panel h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .cl-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .cl-legend span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .cl-key {
    width: 1.1rem;
    height: 0;
    flex: none;
    border-top-width: 3px;
    border-top-style: solid;
  }
  .cl-key--fit {
    border-top-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .cl-key--true {
    border-top-style: dashed;
    border-top-color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .cl-key--asset {
    border: none;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .cl-key--blend {
    border: none;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-link);
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .cl-key--ref {
    border: none;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .cl-readouts {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .cl-readouts {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  .cl-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .cl-stats > div {
    min-width: 0;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .cl-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .cl-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .cl-verdict {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
  }
  .cl-up {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .cl-down {
    color: var(--color-error);
  }
  .cl-fair {
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
</style>
